  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Application Scope**\n\nI\'m focusing on defining the scope for \"Trade2Turkey\'s\" application. It needs to handle export logistics, shipment tracking, and supplier evaluation/verification processes. This is the foundation; the specifics will follow.\n\n\n**Mapping Application Modules**\n\nI\'ve been mapping the application modules to the Standard Operating Procedure. Section A, \"Sourcing,\" breaks down into specific pages: \'Creation Target Specification,\' \'RFQ Submission,\' \'RFQ Matrix,\' \'Product Recipe,\' and costing analyses. The app will embed these into the SOP. Section B deals with alignment & coordination, inventory, and fulfillment. I\'m focusing on the integration points between these modules.\n\n\n**Building Key Features**\n\nNow, I\'m concentrating on the core features. I\'m prioritizing the Supplier Scoring dashboard; it\'s vital for Trade2Turkey. Next up is granular product costing, where every component\'s price is broken down. The Secure Client Portal will allow a real-time update system, for desktop and mobile, for clients. Finally, I\'m thinking about user-friendly data entry to create reports.\n\n\n**Assessing API Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `metadata.json` to define our app\'s core attributes. Updating the `name` to \"Trade2Turkey Logistics\" and the `description` to \"Sourcing, supplier evaluation, costing breakdown, and shipment logistics tracker\" is the immediate next step. I\'m also examining the workspace files \342\200\223 `package.json`, `App.tsx` \342\200\223 to assess package dependencies. I\'m considering using the `gemini_api` skill to create real-time reports and granular costing analyses. I think it could be very beneficial. But, first, I will perform a skill check. Only `firebase-integration` is available.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 901463598
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
