  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Listing Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently compiling a list of project dependencies. I\'ve noted `lucide-react`, `motion`, core React libraries and associated Tailwind utilities. I\'ve just remembered the React Setup guidelines, which remind me that we have a custom server setup.\n\n\n**Considering Architecture Alternatives**\n\nI\'m now weighing the merits of a client-side SPA approach as the default, given its robustness and responsiveness for simulating various features like mock uploads and cost calculations. This architecture would streamline user-friendly data entry and real-time report generation. It seems to work well, and standard React SPA structure is highly robust here, so I\'m investigating it further. I\'m also ensuring compatibility with the existing file structure, specifically `/src/App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Detailing Existing Files**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the existing project files, including `/src/index.css` and `/src/main.tsx`. Next, I\'ll review the SOP data and its structured sections. I\'m focusing on Section A, \"Sourcing,\" and its subsections, such as \"Discovery and Feasibility\" and \"Quotation, Quality and Compliance.\" This detailed section breakdown should help clarify the project scope.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Sections**\n\nI\'m now outlining key dashboard sections. I\'ll need tabs for Section A (Sourcing), Section B (Logistics/Inventory/Fulfillment), and a Supplier Verification Portal/Client View. The latter will provide tracking, certificates, audit reports, and recipe transparency. Within Section A, the dashboard should present the complete SOP list with status updates. Section B will include various sub-processes.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Tools**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive tool design for specific SOP steps. For Step A.A.2, I\'m envisioning an elegant target specification builder for product definition, like dimensions and safety standards. Step A.A.4 demands a customized RFQ submission tool, allowing users to generate and track RFQs. Lastly, Step A.A.6 requires a fully interactive costing breakdown tool showing costs at each step of the value chain. I am aiming for rich, detailed interfaces with excellent user experience. I will include KPI days, owners, and digital storage links for each step.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Tools**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive tool design. I\'m building an RFQ comparison matrix (Step A.B.6) to compare suppliers, highlighting the best option based on weighted metrics. Additionally, I\'m designing a product recipe builder (Step A.B.8) with detailed material ingredient breakdowns, complete with weights, units, scrap rates, and costs. Furthermore, I am implementing a material costing tool (Step A.B.9) to dynamically calculate granular costs for each component, including wastage and overhead, to show the transparent value chain costs, and build a supplier scoring dashboard.\n\n\n**Designing Verification Systems**\n\nI\'m now detailing a supplier verification system with key metrics like Cost (25%), Communication (15%), and Lead Time (20%) using star ratings, risk level, and a comprehensive verification checklist. I\'m also planning a client-facing secure evidence portal, including live container tracking simulations (vessel location, estimated arrival), and a verification and QC document vault for easy viewing and downloads (NDAs, audits, certifications, approvals). I am also designing it to be fully mobile-responsive.\n\n\n**Structuring Project Files**\n\nI am now implementing the modular file structure. I\'m focusing on `/src/types.ts` for all types, `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` for the branded header, and `/src/components/SourcingSOP.tsx` for SOP handling. I am also working on  `/src/components/MinorSheets.tsx` for the sub-tools.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 517676794
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
