  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Initial Sections**\n\nI\'ve finalized `src/types.ts`. Now, the focus shifts to designing the application\'s sections. I\'ve identified two major areas: Sourcing, which contains discovery/feasibility and quotation/compliance subsections. I\'m keen to flesh out the interaction between them.\n\n\n**Building Minor Sheet Links**\n\nI\'m now integrating the minor sheets within the Sourcing SOP. Clicking a sourcing step will trigger an embedded view of its corresponding worksheet. This approach neatly handles both \"redirect\" and \"embed\" requirements, offering a seamless and intuitive user experience with a clear return path. Moving on, I\'m starting to build the Navbar component.\n\n\n**Structuring Application Services**\n\nI\'ve established the primary application services, structuring them as: Sourcing (SOP & Worksheets), Strategic Project Alignment/Logistics, Supplier Scoring/Verification, Stakeholder Portal, and an Executive Report Center. I think this provides a good hierarchical foundation. Next I\'m planning to select icons from `lucide-react` to use within the Navbar component. I\'ll need `Ship`, `Globe`, `Award`, `FileSpreadsheet`, `Users`, and others.\n\n\n"
