    thinking: "**Building Interactive Sheets**\n\nOkay, the navbar is working beautifully! Now, I\'m shifting focus to developing those interactive sheets in `/src/components/MinorSheets.tsx`. I\'m starting to identify the six key components. I\'ve got the first one nailed down: `Creation Target Specification`, which is embedded in A.A.2. I\'m now listing the rest.\n\n\n**Detailing Minor Sheets**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a comprehensive view of the minor sheets now! I\'m focused on making these interactive and powerful. My priorities: real-time syncing and recalculation across the app state, user-friendly forms, and downloadable report generation. I need to make each sheet very practical. So far, the list selector idea feels right, with direct state updates and immutable handlers. Next, I will figure out the user-friendly form fields.\n\n\n**Defining Sheet Components**\n\nI\'ve got the form fields for the target specification pretty much finalized. Now, I\'m diving into the RFQ submission process, specifically the components needed for an RFQ. I\'m prioritizing user input fields like company name, location, and payment terms, so the RFQ document is very practical. Then, I\'ll move on to building the logic to generate the output RFQ document template.\n\n\n**Analyzing Value Chain**\n\nOkay, I\'m now developing a detailed calculation engine for the value chain. I\'m focusing on making a bento grid visual for the cost multipliers. My goal is to allow users to interactively compute and visualize the Total Shipping Cost, Duty/Taxes per Unit, and Overall Landed Cost per Unit, factoring in EXW, logistics, customs, and more. This requires a strong user interface. I\'m also planning to build an interactive component with a visual breakdown chart.\n\n\n\n**Calculating Recipe Costs**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the costing of materials within the active recipe, and focusing on packaging and wastage margins. I\'ve defined the necessary fields: material name, quantity, unit, unit cost, scrap/wastage rate, and supplier. The goal is an interactive calculation of the total raw material ingredients cost. I\'m building a visual breakdown of the active recipe, showing a materials list with wastage calculations for an effective cost. This also dynamically integrates labor, packaging, and production overheads to calculate the final target EXW cost and compares it to a budget limit with a progress bar.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 84
      nanos: 513209034
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
