    thinking: "**Constructing Server.ts**\n\nI\'m currently focused on building the `server.ts` back-end file. My progress includes integrating Express with the Vite middleware, following the provided guidelines. I\'m exploring the specific implementation details, ensuring the correct configuration.\n\n\n**Implementing Server Routes**\n\nI\'ve added the initial Express server setup with a health check route. I\'ve also incorporated the Vite middleware for development and static file serving for production. I\'m now exploring the implementation details for Google OAuth and upload handlers within this server structure, and will consider incorporating information from the `.env.example` to construct the Google OAuth callback URL.\n\n\n**Configuring OAuth Parameters**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on configuring Google OAuth parameters within the server. I\'m focusing on handling the origin dynamically using `process.env.APP_URL` and constructing the authorization URL. The plan includes setting up the necessary scopes for Google Drive and user info: drive, email, and profile. I\'m also preparing the client ID and secret retrieval, considering environment variables.\n\n\n**Adding Simulated Fallback**\n\nI\'m now thinking about how to handle the initial setup for Google Drive integration. If the user hasn\'t set up their Google Client ID and Secret yet, I want to provide a user-friendly instruction screen within the `<GoogleDriveFolder />` component, guiding them to obtain these credentials from the Google Cloud Console. Simultaneously, to ensure immediate usability, I\'ll implement a simulated fallback using mock data that mimics the real API flow. This fallback will keep the app interactive until the user configures their secrets, at which point the real Google Drive API will seamlessly take over.\n\n\n**Implementing Drive File Handling**\n\nI\'m now detailing the logic for Google Drive folder creation and file uploads. I\'ll write the code to create the \"Trade2Turkey Logistics\" root folder if it doesn\'t exist, and then search for or create project and SOP step subfolders within it. The file will then be uploaded to its correct location. I will query the Google Drive API to verify and manage the file structures.\n\n\n**Refining Upload Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Google Drive file upload and folder structure logic. I\'m writing the code to search for or create specific folders (e.g., \".C.7 - Customs Documentation\") within the project and manage the folder\'s mapping in the structure. I\'m using the Google Drive API to query for folder existence, and create them if not found. I\'m now integrating the file upload using the multipart endpoint, and plan to include metadata retrieval. I\'m exploring setting appropriate permissions, like \"anyone with link\" reader access, to make files readily accessible.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am going to create the backend entry point file `/server.ts` using the Express + Vite full-stack template configuration. This server will handle:\n1. Google OAuth 2.0 authorization URL redirection and token exchange.\n2. The B2B Google Drive file upload proxy endpoint, which dynamically creates the project directory hierarchy in Google Drive, uploads physical files, and makes them readable via shared links in the client portal.\n3. Dev and production server hosting with Vite\'s middleware integrated."
