  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Completed Architecture**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased to report the successful completion of the Google Drive physical mapping architecture. Everything built and linted perfectly. The server restarted without a hitch. I\'m now conducting a brief review of the initial requirements, to ensure complete alignment and confirm no vital components were overlooked in the development process.\n\n\n**Confirming Implementation Details**\n\nI\'ve confirmed direct mapping of \"Digital Storing Locations\" to Google Drive folders. The backend now automates folder creation using SOP storage locations, precisely mirroring the Trade2Turkey Logistics structure. Dynamic file retrieval from designated CSV \"Digital Storing Location\" columns is also confirmed. Finally, B2B client access is restricted to read-only access with query limitation tied to `currentProjectId` for security.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have populated actual **Google Drive API (v3) Integration** across the Trade2Turkey portal, linking raw file storage mappings to physical Google Workspace directories while observing security guidelines.\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Design & Architectural Concept\n- **Synced Cloud Credentials Panel**: Introduced a visual badge systems bar tracking active Google Drive authorization states. Sourcing agents can lock in their real Google workspace with a single click, instantly transforming local sandbox slots into living cloud folders.\n- **Physical Drag-and-Drop Integrations**: Rewired the SOP Digital Storing Location upload centers to ingest real binary files seamlessly (PDF reports, RFQ spreadsheets, lab certificates, cargo photoshoot proofs) and pipe them directly into the Google Drive cloud.\n- **Aesthetic Pairings**: Aligned the custom panel elements with the established **Professional Polish** theme\342\200\224utilizing high-contrast status pills, slate color accents, micro-interaction state transitions, and responsive grid layouts.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\223\246 Solution Deliverables\n\n#### 1. Real Google OAuth 2.0 Node/Express Backend (`server.ts`)\n- **Authorization Generator (`/api/auth/google-url`)**: Generates an authoritative Google OAuth 2.0 flow request scope for a popup consent screen.\n- **Callback Swap Handshake (`/auth/callback`)**: Swaps short-lived codes for active workspace access tokens, fetches user profiles, and communicates the active security token back to the React app parent via secure `window.opener.postMessage`.\n- **In-Memory Cache Singleton (`src/lib/driveAuth.ts`)**: Adheres strictly to security rules by keeping active tokens cached purely in-memory rather than unencrypted inside localStorage, ensuring active connection synchronization across all tabs.\n\n#### 2. Fully Automated Multi-Tier Workspace Folder Mapping\n- When a file is uploaded to the SOP panel, the server automatically searches or initializes the corresponding directories in your real Google Drive instance:\n  1. **Root Workspace**: `Trade2Turkey Logistics` (Primary hub).\n  2. **B2B Project isolation**: Re-creates specific project folders, e.g. `PROJ-BEANBAG (ComfortPro Bean Bags)` or `PROJ-VELVET`.\n  3. **Task SOP Subfolder**: Maps the designated SOP column directly as a subfolder, e.g. `B.C.7 - Shared Folder - Cargo Proof Photos`.\n- Uploads the physical binary to its respective target subfolder and configures file sharing permissions to \"Anyone with Link role: Reader\", mapping the document\'s real web view URL back to the portal in real-time.\n\n#### 3. Client Protection & Automated Automation Handshake\n- **Access Isolation**: B2B client modes restrict document clearance strictly to their certified Project ID, preventing sensitive industrial blueprints or supplier quotes from leaking between partners.\n- **Automated SOP Status Hook**: Uploading or dropping a proof sheet automatically changes the task state to **\"Completed\"**, updating the client portal instantly.\n- **Hybrid Sandbox Fallback**: If no custom Google developer secrets are declared, the app smoothly continues operating in \"Offline Sandbox Mode,\" letting you test administrative SOP routines without interruption."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 809504068
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
