      title: "techtarget.com"
    }
    summary: "The phrase \"No location information provided in request side-channel\" is likely a technical error message. To understand its meaning, it\'s helpful to break down the components: \"location information\" and \"side-channel.\"\n\n\"Location information\" refers to data about a physical or geographical position. Errors related to \"no location found\" are commonly encountered in applications that rely on GPS or network-based positioning, such as location-sharing features on smartphones. These issues can stem from a poor GPS signal, weak internet connection, disabled location services, airplane mode, low battery, or software glitches[1][2].\n\nA \"side-channel\" in computer security refers to any information that can be inadvertently leaked by a computer system through its physical implementation rather than its intended communication channels[3][4][5][6]. This leaked information, known as \"side-channel leakage,\" can include timing variations in computations, power consumption, electromagnetic emissions, or even sound[3][4][5][6]. Side-channel attacks exploit these subtle effects to gain unauthorized access to sensitive data, such as cryptographic keys, without directly attacking the cryptographic algorithms themselves[3][7][5][6].\n\nGiven this context, \"No location information provided in request side-channel\" could imply:\n*   A system attempting to provide location data is failing to do so through an expected (possibly unintended or unsecure) channel.\n*   More broadly, it might be an internal system message indicating that a request for location data did not receive the necessary information through the designated data flow or \"channel.\"\n\nWhile the exact meaning can vary depending on the specific system generating the error, it points to a failure in retrieving or transmitting location data through a particular mechanism.\n\nSources:\n[1] [nordvpn.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFlEY77KyVHxIG4j2ny-zm179b5x-RnmF3-MEIWNS4NtsejsryMo4tqOpTpAzpwua1G_8yCHpXXcim9zCjziDwkFL6GoI6l_vJxbZbXSHmDJQH4B9ejJ99H809GiZribHHY7_f4Y1XaGpA3HdQCaw==)\n[2] [itoolab.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGeGPZkJEUR_EDVnjopY_GZgtFkgPmxGKpGcyj0RsEbPe7BxJI2pJvo3uZWaQqgNKB72l6SDEDXfCsz_VsHKtzIv_98qTbT-6ufitaAAZRu6mxBf1c3aUQDUo7IxU8YYamcYGgzl4ErGG1S6-WXDKyRJ0NXnpENWQLIeWluvcvZ5nWWWHtJezs=)\n[3] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEtENZEaNZnq4jZ_5dILud5P4JSB2iciv8Cdd2_yh1S4m22tNuNjsFWQzuqrqs37_RFNWmfcKJsUK7YwXKrIExnaLy0PUKxszZ0yIg22ygKnNbJVG3BMshmElXkEQ2PrEfVTbz2HPN1BMMgyo0=)\n[4] [fortanix.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF1ksfw1PEMCHkVL1upy_UT6r8ScQiFWCvisJp8-ZAYNrPIVVPn4GIt5OUznUroZxwt3Vk-i4ELNrFOYgvtqlLLLH43sAZF8mXPH_VN97degsrox-OH7k0gnLc95tjM-AMI8Duy3VGNmbflINJL1cObQZwv2dM33SeYnpHBhEtuZxijJMHg8TWBIw==)\n[5] [jumpcloud.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG055lHn6hvXfPuHmHM4kFA_whYcmggSDCGSyh_kXyFYjESjnMTZ4U-1uriDRTiUZM8-Y8HdaCyPjdGfE-GRuYiY2dcOa0iFpFTPYa7K0Va0IqbtvIjXPD5MABZt8Ys-fCIJ6YWXf37lc7kbHnBjwpyYFDP7wCtLA==)\n[6] [x-phy.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE4Rvnnzdna5MIa27ApsGJqini8Vk6xxU-bS_chzO6Dd-h-eOQX4pBpZNCSl4n2yZvItuQSzAljJsD3_5fEuRGfEIKPUBjT8BoWG0mm0NSmW8KW7v_U1skcLW53Kz_J_XwqWtzJ9LOt6NE5PZKp3nGr4nUlsLuBHqT7H3Hyk243TU2wEdCUP7WuFRYIDqVi)\n[7] [techtarget.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH5fKUVvbqBsmQoX5Nw2frcnuXygRHdLpcXPI1kgyWF7wd9gqvGUXSK0nEVfyIFi46Bp8E4sXn3Dv5dvcz0yDD74nKZ6gwWyX-qoC7MR9BNozPsK0OIOlv_G2CY5etGLMDko8giAbUYDF_0qXwQCXHJQ3s12TFU_frdg6c6AfNxb-d_cQ==)"
