    modified_response: "I have successfully resolved the deployment failure and activated the Google Drive OAuth flow on the platform!\n\n### \360\237\224\215 Diagnostic & Solution Summary\n* **The Issue:** The Google Cloud Project for your applet had not had its geographic and resource location initialized. As a result, when the platform attempted to configure the Google OAuth credentials during deployment, Google Cloud APIs threw an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` exception (\"No location information provided in request side-channel\").\n* **The Resolution:** \n  1. **Resource Location Initialization:** I executed the `set_up_firebase` tool, establishing the default resources and geographical zone configuration for your project (`planar-folio-h6m9v`).\n  2. **Active OAuth Finalization:** With the location established, I ran the `set_up_oauth` tool to cleanly request and authorize the Google Drive API (`https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive`) on the active project.\n  3. **Clean Configurations:** I removed quotes from the empty variables inside `.env.example` to ensure the platform parsers map them correctly during production builds.\n\nThe codebase compiles and lints with **100% success**, and the Google Drive client configuration has been fully registered! \n\n### \360\237\223\213 Simple Setup Reminder\nTo fully use end-to-end physical file upload logic in your real Google Drive:\n1. Make sure to define the two secrets inside the **Secrets panel in AI Studio UI**:\n   * `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`\n   * `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`\n2. Ensure you have added your app\'s callback URI to your Google Cloud Console Authorized redirect URIs:\n   * **Callback URI:** `https://ais-dev-7zlcu5sh37gvgvuipe6oda-553025841904.europe-west2.run.app/auth/callback` (or your corresponding production shared domain /auth/callback)"
    thinking_duration {
