    thinking: "**Evaluating the Implementation**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the aesthetic match! I\'m now digging into `/src/App.tsx`, focusing on import statements for custom types, credentials, and `LoginScreen`, implementing session management, and building out the logic for `currentUser` and `activeProjectId`, and also how to handle a higher-order component.\n\n\n**Designing the \"Admin Desk\"**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to designing the \"Admin Client Accounts Desk\" component. My current thought is to create a dynamic drawer for owner/admin roles. I\'m focusing on features: viewing all clients, adding corporate clients (including defaults), and the ability to log in/inspect a client\'s workspace. I\'ll need to modify `/src/App.tsx` from line 112 onwards. I\'m estimating the file size to grow considerably.\n\n\n**Reviewing App\'s Sub-Views**\n\nI\'m now diving back into `/src/App.tsx`, specifically lines 200-299 to ensure a comprehensive understanding of how sub-views are called within the layout. I\'m carefully scrutinizing the props passed, to ensure I\'m not missing any critical variables or mismatches (like `rfqs`, `valueChain`, `inventory`, etc.), so that the component can be as flexible as possible. My focus is on ensuring consistency. I noticed I had already seen lines 201-299 earlier.\n\n\n**Analyzing Component Render Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the conditional rendering of components, specifically `SourcingSOP` and `LogisticsSOP`. I\'m verifying the logic for passing props such as `steps`, `setSteps`, `currentProjectId`, and `canSwitchProject`. I\'m paying close attention to how these props affect component behavior and data flow, and how the rendered component will render properly.\n\n\n"
