    thinking: "**Considering Visual Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the company logo visually within the application. An actual image was provided, so I\'m thinking about creating a high-fidelity component to represent it exactly. I will need to consider rendering this logo as faithfully as possible.\n\n\n**Designing Brand Logo Component**\n\nI\'m now in the process of designing the `BrandLogo.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on supporting different sizes and styles. I\'ve analyzed the logo, noting the circular, glowing blue-cyan globe with network lines and the \"Trade2Turkey\" branding. I\'m carefully considering the color codes for each part and how to integrate the \"Digital Workflows, Disciplined Sourcing\" and \"T2T\" text elements. The plan is to create a reusable component for consistent branding, replacing existing SVG placeholders. It should be able to accept size options like `\'sm\'`, `\'md\'`, etc.\n\n\n**Refining Component Visuals**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual implementation of the `BrandLogo` component. I\'m focusing on rendering both the icon and full branding inline, exactly as in the uploaded image. My goal is to create a stunning SVG representation of the bright, light-blue node globe with its transparent orbits, ensuring a professional, modern B2B tech aesthetic. I\'m paying close attention to the specific color codes and font styles to create a perfect replica of the text block.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a unified, high-fidelity React component for the Trade2Turkey company logo inside `/src/components/BrandLogo.tsx`. This component will reproduce the beautiful blue-cyan constellation globe with glowing vertices and orbits, and the official typography (\"Trade2Turkey\", slogan, and \"T2T\") configured to scale elegantly with different size presets across systems."
